    "content": "Amy Madigan won Best Supporting Actress at the 98th Academy Awards (2026) for her role as Aunt Gladys in Weapons. She defeated a competitive field that included Elle Fanning and Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas (Sentimental Value), Wunmi Mosaku (Sinners), and Teyana Taylor (One Battle After Another), setting a record for the longest gap (40 years) between nominations. Watch Amy Madigan's acceptance speech for her Best Supporting Actress win:03:27OscarsYouTube • Mar 15, 2026 03:27 2026 Best Supporting Actress Nominees: Winner: Amy Madigan – Weapons Elle Fanning – Sentimental Value Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas – Sentimental Value Wunmi Mosaku – Sinners Teyana Taylor – One Battle After Another Key Highlights: Record-Breaking Win: Madigan’s win for Weapons came 40 years after her first nomination in 1986 (Twice in a Lifetime). Contender Field: Teyana Taylor entered the Oscars with wins from the Golden Globes and Critics Choice Awards. Multiple Nods: Sentimental Value secured two slots in this category with nominations for both Elle Fanning and Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas.",
